&gt; That's not how a printer with a fax/modem works.<p>It is how at least one of them works, and how I assumed all of them work. <a href="http://www.whoopis.com/howtos/laserwriter16-600/LaserWriter_16_600_PSPrintr.pdf" rel="nofollow">http://www.whoopis.com/howtos/laserwriter16-600/LaserWriter_...</a>:</p><p><i>“FaxOptions    Dictionary    This dictionary contains parameters that direct fax transmissions from a PostScript language program. Refer to “Fax Parameters” on page 29 for further information about FaxOptions defaults and the keys found in this dictionary”</i></p><p>Google tells me this is what you needed in your PostScript file to send a fax:</p><p></p><pre><code>  &lt;&lt;
    /OutputDevice /Fax
    /FaxOptions &lt;&lt;
      /DialCallee (555-0199)
    &gt;&gt;
  &gt;&gt; setpagedevice

</code></pre>
And I don’t think Apple was unique in having fax support in their PostScript. <a href="https://web.mit.edu/PostScript/Adobe/Documents/5001.DSC_Spec.pdf" rel="nofollow">https://web.mit.edu/PostScript/Adobe/Documents/5001.DSC_Spec...</a> mentions faxing, too (but doesn’t appear to say how to accomplish it)

